    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d439-a5">

                <pb facs="0787" n="691" xml:id="pg691"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5 in No. 95]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Seward to Mr. Bingham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-05-30"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 30,
                        1874</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 22.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have had the honor to receive your
                    dispatch of the 18th instant in regard to the expedition to Formosa. I have sent
                    letters to the appropriate consuls in China embodying the information contained
                    in your dispatch and saying that I think that any steps which they may take to
                    discourage, or, within the provisions of law, to prevent our people from taking
                    part in such expedition will meet the warm approval of our Government.</p>
                <p>I have sent a copy of your letter to Dr. Williams.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GEORGE F. SEWARD,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Consul-General</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
